1
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,080
Try looking at it from a distance.

2
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone with no money, come to me.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I don't have any either, so don't you worry.

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,780
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,280
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:42,780
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,220
Look, even Akaneru, burning away,
will work out somehow in time.

10
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:27,440
You get it, right? Got it, got it. Once
you understand, gather round and follow me.

11
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:52,880
Nice weather

12
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:55,280
It's the height of summer, isn't it.

13
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,120
Really.

14
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,280
Oh my.

15
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,900
Ryo-chan's yawn got caught on camera.

16
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,540
That's dangerous, two people on one bike!

17
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:14,640
You two.

18
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:19,960
Here you go.

19
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,660
Ryo-chan, you're quick.

20
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,920
You two, riding double on a bicycle is dangerous,
so you can't do that.

21
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,940
Yeah, yeah, got it.

22
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:36,660
You don't seem the least bit remorseful.

23
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,800
Sounds like you're just saying the words.

24
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:45,220
I'm not at the age to sit still for a lecture.
You're awfully understanding today, Ryo-chan.

25
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:51,060
I just remembered, watching those kids.
Remembered what?

26
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,940
Found it, here it is. What's this scar?

27
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:00,100
Well?

28
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:05,160
It's from when I was a junior high schooler,
just like those kids.

29
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,820
Asakusa Shonen Gurettai

30
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:22,140
The World Expo held for
the first time in Japan

31
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:26,560
with every pavilion packed daily
with visitors from all over the world,

32
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,460
is showing an enormous crowd.

33
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,440
Truly, a hello from
every country in the world.

34
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,760
Within this World Expo,

35
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,700
The World Expo

36
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:38,600
I really ought to see this at least once.

37
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:42,560
But it's in Osaka,
so it's a long trip by train.

38
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,100
It'd be nice if they held it at the Sensō-ji grounds or Hanayashiki,
since that's close.

39
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,440
Before we pick,

40
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:54,600
Hanayashiki's too small. They could
only fit one paribilion or so, right?

41
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,760
It's "pavilion," not "paribilion," Dad.

42
00:03:58,500 --> 00:03:59,140
Shut up.

43
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,420
It caught, it caught!

44
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,420
Hey, Toppe, Chikichi, you two get on too.

45
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,140
Are you okay, Kankichi?

46
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:12,900
It's Uncle's motorbike,
so if you break it, it'll be a big deal.

47
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,300
Heji-heji, get on quickly.

48
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:17,740
Okay.

49
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,540
Can you actually drive it?

50
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:24,320
Leave it to me,
it's just a bicycle with a motor, right?

51
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,740
Let's go, departing!

52
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,980
Easy, easy.

53
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,220
What do you two think you're doing?

54
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,260
Oh no.

55
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:47,060
Stop! You can't ride it like that!

56
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,200
Kankichi, this is bad, stop!

57
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:52,260
So what if it is?

58
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,600
I don't know how to stop it.

59
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:28,600
Uuuuuuuuuuuuugh...

60
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,840
So what happened?

61
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:41,420
Luckily,
I got caught in a fishing boat's net.

62
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:46,500
If not, I'd have been swept
all the way out to Tokyo Bay.

63
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,040
Of course, I got a severe scolding, though.

64
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:53,040
The young police officer back
then was a really nice guy.

65
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,160
Right?

66
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:58,258
Back in the old days, he'd take us
for rides on his motorcycle one by one,

67
00:05:58,308 --> 00:06:00,960
zooming us around the neighborhood.

68
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,500
Hey, next time, give me a ride!

69
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,560
That time it was my turn, remember!

70
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,500
Now that you mention it, that happened too.

71
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:19,780
Hey, Dad, let's get a color TV too.

72
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,080
Color? You idiot!

73
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,560
A tsukudani shop like ours
doesn't need a color TV!

74
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:25,740
But that's not fair!

75
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,740
Tsuyoshi's family and Satoru's
family both bought one!

76
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,460
More than half the class
has color TVs already!

77
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:32,320
Hmph!

78
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:36,280
Back then, that
"COLOR" label that appeared at the edge of the screen

79
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,340
looked like a taunt on black-and-white sets,
you know.

80
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:40,360
Hey, Dad!

81
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:41,840
Shut up!

82
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,660
I don't need any color!

83
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:46,860
If you watch that stuff,
your brain turns into color!

84
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:47,840
Tch...

85
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,000
But...

86
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:54,100
There was one show I
just had to see in color.

87
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,840
What show was that?

88
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,000
Well, it was this one...

89
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:01,640
For us who hit puberty back then,
it was a legendary show.

90
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:09,420
We desperately wanted to see it in color,

91
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,700
so we made a deal with the electrician's son

92
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,900
and broke into the shop at night.

93
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:20,300
Hey, Shinji,
you sure this is going to be okay?

94
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,540
As long as we're quiet, it's fine.
Our family goes to bed early.

95
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,420
Alright.

96
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:41,580
Shinpirobonto!

97
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,960
Yeah, it's different from Canada.

98
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,620
Just as I thought, someone doesn't want to.

99
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:19,340
There it is!

100
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,360
You bastard!

101
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,440
You lot!

102
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:26,840
Yes!

103
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:31,220
This one.

104
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:45,420
What happened?

105
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:51,320
H-hey, wait!

106
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:52,000
Stop!

107
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,340
I survived!

108
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,400
You can't run anymore!

109
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:03,540
You're

110
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,780
Shinji,

111
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:08,060
being taken to the police box

112
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:10,060
was your fifth time this year

113
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,660
This year?

114
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:15,260
Five times in one year?

115
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:18,560
How many times have you
actually been at the police box?

116
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:20,480
Fifteen times.

117
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:23,240
Maybe it was sixteen.

118
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,400
Well, that's a minor detail.

119
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,500
Who cares about that anyway?

120
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:31,700
What else did you have to put up with?

121
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:35,540
Well, the one that
stands out in my memory is

122
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,020
Please pay attention.

123
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,900
Hey, was it worth buying the color TV, Dad?

124
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,220
W-well, yeah.

125
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,000
Honestly.

126
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:57,400
All you talk about is the Olympics,
the Olympics.

127
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:00,540
You're glued to the TV
from morning till night.

128
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,360
Those two...

129
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,600
It's getting farther, it's getting farther!

130
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,380
We did it!

131
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,380
Japan's Hinomaru Flying Squadron!

132
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:23,480
Yay!

133
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,640
Charged right in!

134
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,120
As expected,

135
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,520
at the Sapporo Olympics,

136
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,940
had us all completely captivated.

137
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,340
Here we go!

138
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:39,980
Chikichi!

139
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,340
Oi, me!

140
00:10:42,180 --> 00:11:10,200
Yeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeah... good, good, good,
good, good, good, good, good, good, good, good!

141
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:17,500
Imitating the Flying Squadron, and now it's done!
A magnificent ski jump, right? Over here!

142
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:22,040
Satisfied! Let's slide down right away

143
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:29,580
Who can fly the farthest today!
The winner gets three bento boxes, so there!

144
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:32,780
Number one, Toppe, is going now!

145
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:34,880
Guh!

146
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:35,340
Hah!

147
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,000
Ohhh!

148
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:40,960
Nyaaah!

149
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,680
Tick!

150
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:44,220
Landing failed!

151
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,460
Hahaha, you're terrible at this.

152
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:47,680
This is how you do it.

153
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:50,500
Now, Kasaya Kankichi!

154
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,320
I'm aiming to beat the record.

155
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,220
Yes!

156
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,020
Hyaaah!

157
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:58,080
Wheee!

158
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,260
How about that!

159
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:27,680
Dozens of pigs ran wild
through the streets of Asakusa.

160
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,140
Hahaha!

161
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,840
Naturally,
we ended up in the hands of the police,

162
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,980
and Dad really gave us a good scolding.

163
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,480
"Causing trouble for everyone like that!"

164
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,080
That's when I'd really
reflect on what I did.

165
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,740
Ugh, it's cold.

166
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:45,100
I'm starving.

167
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,400
Hey, did they kick you out again?

168
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:50,860
Here you go.

169
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,440
Thanks, officer.

170
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,340
That's good.

171
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,020
Don't rush like that. Here.

172
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,660
Falling into the river on a
three-person motorbike ride,

173
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:22,400
sneaking into an electronics shop
and getting mistaken for a thief,

174
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:26,100
and stampeding pigs by imitating a jump,
and so on!

175
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:30,060
Honestly, Ryo-chan's middle school days were a total mess,
weren't they?

176
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:35,300
We also did a chicken
race on bicycles back then!

177
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:39,240
The opponents were the punks
from the next-door middle school.

178
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,340
Ready, Kankichi?

179
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:45,460
Yeah. The loser has to do whatever the
winner says for the whole day, got it?

180
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:46,880
I know!

181
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,040
Don't you dare chicken out!

182
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:49,400
Good luck, Kankichi!

183
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:52,300
The honor of Daimon
Junior High is on the line!

184
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:54,500
I know! Leave it to me!

185
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,520
Alright, here we go!

186
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:59,880
Whoever bails first or
hits the brakes loses!

187
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,160
Ready...

188
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:05,500
Go!

189
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,920
Go on, Kankichi!

190
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:19,100
Aaaaaaah!

191
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:29,140
Aaaaaah!

192
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:30,180
Aaaaaah!

193
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:41,920
Aaaaaah!

194
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,620
Aaaaaah!

195
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:48,820
Aaaaaah!

196
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:49,320
Aaaaaah!

197
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,480
Aaaaaah!

198
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:54,080
Eeeeeeh!

199
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:04,820
Aaaaaah!

200
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,820
Are you all right?

201
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:10,440
Eeeeeeh!

202
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:15,020
I have to admit,
I was in real trouble back then.

203
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:16,580
With problems like that...

204
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,340
All we can do is laugh.

205
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,280
And there were others too.

206
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:21,900
There's more?

207
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,880
I'm almost scared to hear this.

208
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:28,680
Most of the students at our school were rather meek,
you see.

209
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:31,340
We were targeted by bad
students from all over the place.

210
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,980
One day, I found one of our students
being harassed by those punks.

211
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,740
Run away while you can!

212
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:54,100
Yeah.

213
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,460
Hey, it's you again?

214
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,640
Hehehehehe!

215
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:17,040
You even went and got me hurt!

216
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:21,000
No matter how much energy you have to spare,
you've gone too far.

217
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,040
But...

218
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,520
Don't you "but" me.

219
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,580
That hurt.

220
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:25,840
It's not a joke, you know.

221
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:27,060
Quit whacking me!

222
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:28,720
It's because you don't listen when I talk.

223
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,360
You're the kind of guy who

224
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,540
should be sent to
Gokurakuji to be made a monk.

225
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:33,940
No!

226
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,880
I don't want to be a monk, I said!

227
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:39,280
Well, there were three of them against him,
after all.

228
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,200
Three against one!

229
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,600
Everybody!

230
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:47,580
Hey, Kankichi-kun. Do you know the saying,
"A hot temper is a losing temper"?

231
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:49,240
A hot temper is a losing temper?

232
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:52,900
It means losing your
temper will cost you dearly.

233
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:56,040
Fighting doesn't get you anything, does it?

234
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,580
But we can't just run away!

235
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:04,140
But those words carried more weight

236
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:06,120
than I'd thought, a thousand times over.

237
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:07,840
What do you mean?

238
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:12,440
He was aiming to become champion, you know.

239
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:15,200
Champion?

240
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:21,400
He did boxing?

241
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,000
Yeah.

242
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:32,440
He debuted in high school
with five wins and no losses.

243
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:34,940
He was expected to go far,

244
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:38,360
but right before the East
Japan novice championship final,

245
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:43,680
while out on a night run,

246
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,220
he got picked on by five punks.

247
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,780
So what happened then?

248
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:16,360
He ended up with a compound
fracture in his wrist.

249
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,620
He had to give up on his
dream of becoming champion.

250
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:27,860
If I'd had a bit more sense back then,
I would have run away.

251
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,480
It was only later that I realized
that was the right decision.

252
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:33,740
But you know,

253
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:39,960
Fine, I'm never fighting again.

254
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:45,400
I promise. So you said that, Kankichi-kun

255
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:03,320
Heh. Scared, are you?

256
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,640
I'm not scared at all!

257
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,360
What?!

258
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:13,160
Don't you get cocky with me!

259
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:20,660
Ugh, I'm not scared of you! But

260
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:23,700
A hot temper only costs you, Kankichi.

261
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:28,380
I promised not to fight!

262
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,180
Hehehe, you coward!

263
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:32,560
Hehehe.

264
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,720
Grr...

265
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:38,960
Hmph! Get down on your knees and beg!
Then I'll let you off!

